VulkanNetwork - portable UDP sockets plus reliable ordered-independent message transport.
Header network/network.hpp. Uses C++17 and WinSock2 or POSIX sockets, no Vulkan.
host owns a socket and one reliable stream channel per endpoint. Client and
server use the same API: start(port), send(peer, bytes), pump(), pop(delivery).
Channels support datagram fragmentation, checksums, duplicate rejection,
fragment acknowledgments, bounded queue/window and timed retransmission.
Application owns encoding, authorization, congestion/bandwidth policy, and
game-specific message types. Traffic is unencrypted; use a secure transport
when sending confidential or untrusted traffic. Both endpoints must agree
on stream::settings.mtu. Bounds are configurable but throughput is limited
by hardware, network and CPU. Do not interpret host as internet security,
DDoS protection, NAT traversal, or a TCP/QUIC replacement.
